{"files": [{"id": 42161527, "name": "pgen.1010903.s028.xlsx", "size": 10706, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/42161527", "supplied_md5": "d459efed055dfb91efc221f934042837", "computed_md5": "d459efed055dfb91efc221f934042837", "mimetype": "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 842833, "full_name": "Karine Normandin", "first_name": "Karine", "last_name": "Normandin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 126532, "full_name": "Jasmin Coulombe-Huntington", "first_name": "Jasmin", "last_name": "Coulombe-Huntington", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 16892359, "full_name": "Corinne St-Denis", "first_name": "Corinne", "last_name": "St-Denis", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 16892362, "full_name": "Alexandre Bernard", "first_name": "Alexandre", "last_name": "Bernard", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9592382, "full_name": "Mohammed Bourouh", "first_name": "Mohammed", "last_name": "Bourouh", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 470436, "full_name": "Thierry Bertomeu", "first_name": "Thierry", "last_name": "Bertomeu", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1118, "full_name": "Mike Tyers", "first_name": "Mike", "last_name": "Tyers", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Mike_Tyers", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 73964, "full_name": "Vincent Archambault", "first_name": "Vincent", "last_name": "Archambault", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Vincent_Archambault", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/dataset/S5_Fig_Numerical_Data_/24044767", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<div><p>Polo-like kinase 1 (PLK1) is a serine/threonine kinase required for mitosis and cytokinesis. As cancer cells are often hypersensitive to partial PLK1 inactivation, chemical inhibitors of PLK1 have been developed and tested in clinical trials. However, these small molecule inhibitors alone are not completely effective. PLK1 promotes numerous molecular and cellular events in the cell division cycle and it is unclear which of these events most crucially depend on PLK1 activity. We used a CRISPR-based genome-wide screening strategy to identify genes whose inactivation enhances cell proliferation defects upon partial chemical inhibition of PLK1. Genes identified encode proteins that are functionally linked to PLK1 in multiple ways, most notably factors that promote centromere and kinetochore function. Loss of the kinesin KIF18A or the outer kinetochore protein SKA1 in PLK1-compromised cells resulted in mitotic defects, activation of the spindle assembly checkpoint and nuclear reassembly defects. We also show that PLK1-dependent CENP-A loading at centromeres is extremely sensitive to partial PLK1 inhibition. Our results suggest that partial inhibition of PLK1 compromises the integrity and function of the centromere/kinetochore complex, rendering cells hypersensitive to different kinetochore perturbations. We propose that KIF18A is a promising target for combinatorial therapies with PLK1 inhibitors.</p></div>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 10706, "created_date": "2023-08-28T17:33:58Z", "modified_date": "2023-09-08T18:01:48Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["xlink \"> polo", "wide screening strategy", "threonine kinase required", "spindle assembly checkpoint", "like kinase 1", "cell division cycle", "compromised cells resulted", "nuclear reassembly defects", "different kinetochore perturbations", "rendering cells hypersensitive", "partial plk1 inactivation", "partial plk1 inhibition", "partial inhibition", "cancer cells", "often hypersensitive", "mitotic defects", "kinetochore complex", "plk1 compromises", "plk1 activity", "results suggest", "promising target", "notably factors", "multiple ways", "genetic enhancers", "functionally linked", "extremely sensitive", "dependent cenp", "crucially depend", "completely effective", "combinatorial therapies", "clinical trials", "chemical inhibitors", "based genome", "also show"], "keywords": ["xlink \"> polo", "wide screening strategy", "threonine kinase required", "spindle assembly checkpoint", "like kinase 1", "cell division cycle", "compromised cells resulted", "nuclear reassembly defects", "different kinetochore perturbations", "rendering cells hypersensitive", "partial plk1 inactivation", "partial plk1 inhibition", "partial inhibition", "cancer cells", "often hypersensitive", "mitotic defects", "kinetochore complex", "plk1 compromises", "plk1 activity", "results suggest", "promising target", "notably factors", "multiple ways", "genetic enhancers", "functionally linked", "extremely sensitive", "dependent cenp", "crucially depend", "completely effective", "combinatorial therapies", "clinical trials", "chemical inhibitors", "based genome", "also show"], "categories": [{"id": 4, "title": "Biochemistry", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 12, "title": "Cell Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 13, "title": "Genetics", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 14, "title": "Molecular Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 19, "title": "Pharmacology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 873, "title": "Chemical Sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 734, "title": "Biological Sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 61, "title": "Developmental Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 64, "title": "Cancer", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 128, "title": "Hematology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}], "references": ["https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903"], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Normandin, Karine; Coulombe-Huntington, Jasmin; St-Denis, Corinne; Bernard, Alexandre; Bourouh, Mohammed; Bertomeu, Thierry; et al. (2023). S5 Fig Numerical Data.. PLOS Genetics. Dataset. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903.s028", "related_materials": [{"id": 147166351, "identifier": "10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903", "title": "Genetic enhancers of partial PLK1 inhibition reveal hypersensitivity to kinetochore perturbations", "relation": "IsSupplementTo", "identifier_type": "DOI", "is_linkout": true, "link": "https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903"}], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "id": 24044767, "title": "S5 Fig Numerical Data.", "doi": "10.1371/journal.pgen.1010903.s028", "handle": "", "url": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/24044767", "published_date": "2023-08-28T17:33:58Z", "thumb": "", "defined_type": 3, "defined_type_name": "dataset", "group_id": 98, "url_private_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/account/articles/24044767", "url_public_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/24044767", "url_private_html": "https://figshare.com/account/articles/24044767", "url_public_html": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/dataset/S5_Fig_Numerical_Data_/24044767", "timeline": {"posted": "2023-08-28T17:33:58", "publisherPublication": "2023-08-28T18:01:37", "firstOnline": "2023-08-28"}, "resource_title": "Genetic enhancers of partial PLK1 inhibition reveal hypersensitivity to kinetochore perturbations", "resource_doi": "10.1371/journal.pge